For example, let's say you want to check if the number 31 is prime. The function will return `False` because 31 is not divisible by 2 or 3. But if we try to check if 31 is prime using this function, it would return `True`, which isn't what we want. So, we need to add an additional check at the end to make sure the loop only goes up to the square root of `n`.
